  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>partialcorri</keyword>
  <short_description>Partial correlation coefficients adjusted for internal variables.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>rho = partialcorri(Y, X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>rho = partialcorri(Y, X, Z)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[rho, pval] = partialcorri(...)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[rho, pval] = partialcorri(..., Name, Value)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>partialcorri</b> computes partial correlations between each column of <b>Y</b> and each column of <b>X</b>, adjusting for the remaining columns of <b>X</b>.</p>
    <p>When <b>Z</b> is supplied, both <b>X</b> and <b>Y</b> are additionally controlled for <b>Z</b>. Supported options are <b>Type</b>, <b>Rows</b>, and <b>Tail</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = randn(20, 3);
Y = randn(20, 2);
rho = partialcorri(Y, X)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
